DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Condition variables are used in conjunction with mutexes to wait for con‐
     ditions to occur.  Condition variables are created with ccvv__iinniitt(), where
     _c_v_p is a pointer to space for a _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_v, and _d_e_s_c is a pointer to a
     null-terminated character string that describes the condition variable.
     Condition variables are destroyed with ccvv__ddeessttrrooyy().  Threads wait on
     condition variables by calling ccvv__wwaaiitt(), ccvv__wwaaiitt__ssiigg(),
     ccvv__wwaaiitt__uunnlloocckk(), ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt(), or ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg().  Threads unblock
     waiters by calling ccvv__ssiiggnnaall() to unblock one waiter, or ccvv__bbrrooaaddccaasstt()
     or ccvv__bbrrooaaddccaassttpprrii() to unblock all waiters.  In addition to waking wait‐
     ers, ccvv__bbrrooaaddccaassttpprrii() ensures that all of the waiters have a priority of
     at least _p_r_i by raising the priority of any threads that do not.
     ccvv__wwmmeessgg() returns the description string of _c_v_p, as set by the initial
     call to ccvv__iinniitt().

     The _l_o_c_k argument is a pointer to either a mutex(9), rwlock(9), or sx(9)
     lock.  A mutex(9) argument must be initialized with MTX_DEF and not
     MTX_SPIN.  A thread must hold _l_o_c_k before calling ccvv__wwaaiitt(),
     ccvv__wwaaiitt__ssiigg(), ccvv__wwaaiitt__uunnlloocckk(), ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt(), or ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg().
     When a thread waits on a condition, _l_o_c_k is atomically released before
     the thread is blocked, then reacquired before the function call returns.
     In addition, the thread will fully drop the _G_i_a_n_t mutex (even if re‐
     cursed) while the it is suspended and will reacquire the _G_i_a_n_t mutex be‐
     fore the function returns.  The ccvv__wwaaiitt__uunnlloocckk() function does not reac‐
     quire the lock before returning.  Note that the _G_i_a_n_t mutex may be speci‐
     fied as _l_o_c_k.  However, _G_i_a_n_t may not be used as _l_o_c_k for the
     ccvv__wwaaiitt__uunnlloocckk() function.  All waiters must pass the same _l_o_c_k in con‐
     junction with _c_v_p.

     When ccvv__wwaaiitt(), ccvv__wwaaiitt__ssiigg(), ccvv__wwaaiitt__uunnlloocckk(), ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt(), and
     ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg() unblock, their calling threads are made runnable.
     ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt() and ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg() wait for at most _t_i_m_o / HZ seconds
     before being unblocked and returning EWOULDBLOCK; otherwise, they return
     0.  ccvv__wwaaiitt__ssiigg() and ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg() return prematurely with a value
     of EINTR or ERESTART if a signal is caught, or 0 if signaled via
     ccvv__ssiiggnnaall() or ccvv__bbrrooaaddccaasstt().

     ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssbbtt() and ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg__ssbbtt() functions take _s_b_t argument
     instead of _t_i_m_o.  It allows to specify relative or absolute unblock time
     with higher resolution in form of _s_b_i_n_t_i_m_e___t.  The parameter _p_r allows to
     specify wanted absolute event precision.  The parameter _f_l_a_g_s allows to
     pass additional ccaalllloouutt__rreesseett__ssbbtt() flags.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, ccvv__wwaaiitt__ssiigg(), ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt(), and ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg() re‐
     turn 0.  Otherwise, a non-zero error code is returned.

     ccvv__wwmmeessgg() returns the description string that was passed to ccvv__iinniitt().

EERRRROORRSS
     ccvv__wwaaiitt__ssiigg() and ccvv__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt__ssiigg() will fail if:

     [EINTR]            A signal was caught and the system call should be in‐
                        terrupted.

     [ERESTART]         A signal was caught and the system call should be
